        "Consumer energy resource (CER) uptake in Horizon Power's footprint has historically been low compared with the network administered by Western Power. We estimate that approximately 13% of private dwellings across Port Hedland and South Hedland have rooftop solar installed, compared with around one in three statewide. Several factors have contributed to this: hard caps were placed on solar installations to manage grid stability, particularly in microgrids, regional and remote communities are served by a thinner installer market, higher system costs, and stricter structural requirements owing to the region's exposure to tropical cyclones.",
